data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1399,"item_id":"fc_0ba2850fbf4425dd016adb210cda2881919d1fa7d833236578","output_index":3,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"inference\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"packet_sha256\\\":\\\"a70b0aa80155e9b6356beedf2a844e6fbb5e13c3f04688255e8d17d3c08ebecd\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"UNVERIFIED\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Fresh packet-only mathematical review of the supplied prose finds no unsupported implication in R001. The packet itself supplies all three permitted inputs and the argument explicitly gives the compact-support, differentiation-under-the-integral, integration-by-parts, and orthogonality reasoning. The packet_replay check remains UNVERIFIED: this context reviewed only the packet and Yui rules, but no separately verifiable carrier/isolation execution evidence or independently computed packet hash is available, so I do not certify the required replay receipt.\\\",\\\"checks\\\":{\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"H001 supplies unit norm, H002 supplies the pointwise acceleration-as-scalar-multiple condition, and H003 supplies uniform spatial constancy outside a compact set over each compact time interval. R001 lists and uses precisely these permitted premises; the instantiations described in the prose are compatible.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs/0/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/1/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/2/statement\\\",\\\"/inference/inputs\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1/uses\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2/uses\\\"]},\\\"argument\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"S001 constructs a compact time interval around arbitrary r0. S002 obtains common compact spatial support from H003, uses smoothness and compactness for integrability and uniform continuity, and explains the FTC difference-quotient argument yielding differentiation of E under the integral. S003 gives the product-rule energy derivative, compact-support integration by parts with Fubini justified by continuous compact support, and uses differentiated unit norm plus H002 to make the integrand vanish. These steps suffice for the claimed result.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2/text\\\"]},\\\"dependency_accounting\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"H003 is used for the common spatial support; H001 and H002 are used for the vanishing energy derivative. F001 is locally proved and used only to choose J. Compactness, FTC, uniform continuity, Fubini, and finite-dimensional differentiation are explained in the argument rather than treated as imported theorem inputs. No other substantive external premise is apparent.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/0/produces/0\\\"]},\\\"output\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"For arbitrary positive r0 the argument establishes integrability of e(·,r0), differentiability of E there, and derivative zero; S004 universalizes over positive times and explicitly disclaims endpoint assertions. This matches P's statement and definitions.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/output/statement\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\"]},\\\"scope\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"r0 is arbitrary and remains in scope through S004. J and C_J are chosen from the local existence facts and used only within the argument; neither witness escapes into the output. No temporary assumption requiring discharge is introduced.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/locals/0\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/1\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/2\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\"]},\\\"applicability\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"There are no E/M inputs or source-theorem applications. H003 is applied to the compact interval J whose existence is established locally; H002 is used pointwise at the relevant x,r and its existential scalar conclusion is all that is needed. H001 applies to the same map and time.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/applications\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2/text\\\",\\\"/inputs/1/statement\\\"]},\\\"statement_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The input statements, definitions and output state the needed domains and conditions: smooth u on positive times, unit norm, equation with componentwise spatial Laplacian, compact support condition on each compact time interval, and energy density/integral. The argument's uses of derivatives, compact support, and time interval are understandable from these statements and definitions without producer proofs.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs/0/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/1/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/2/statement\\\",\\\"/definitions/0/definition\\\",\\\"/definitions/1/definition\\\",\\\"/definitions/2/definition\\\",\\\"/output/statement\\\"]},\\\"object_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"R001's actual named mathematical objects are declared as parameters, primitives, definitions, binders, or local witnesses. r0 is introduced arbitrarily; J is supported by F001; C_J is supplied by H003. The scalar in H002 is an existential pointwise witness used only through the stated scalar-multiple conclusion, so no selected free scalar object is needed. No undeclared mathematical object affecting the inference is apparent.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/parameters\\\",\\\"/logic/primitives\\\",\\\"/definitions\\\",\\\"/inference/locals\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2/text\\\"]},\\\"dependency_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Factual uses in S001 derive from positive r0 and elementary interval construction; S002's support claim traces to H003 and its local F001; S003 traces to H001 and H002 and the prior differentiability/integral identity established in S002. S004 uses the arbitrary choice of r0. No ancestor proof or unlisted premise is needed.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\"]},\\\"packet_replay\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"UNVERIFIED\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"This review was conducted in the current context using the supplied packet and Yui procedure, with no other mathematical/source material read. However, no separately verifiable carrier/isolation execution evidence is supplied, and the packet hash was taken from its field rather than independently computed. I therefore do not certify a fresh-carrier replay receipt.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/packet_sha256\\\",\\\"/warning\\\",\\\"/inference\\\"]}},\\\"findings\\\":[]}\"}"}

